  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes the probability of achieving any favorable (i.e., positive) outcome and disregards differences in outcome magnitudes. It would favor Lottery B due to its 90% chance of a positive outcome versus A’s 45%. However, the individual chose Lottery A, citing the higher payout and accepting the lower probability as part of a riskier strategy. This indicates that the individual did not treat outcome differences as negligible—on the contrary, the higher payout was a decisive factor. Furthermore, the individual’s justification is based on a trade-off between risk and reward, not on maximizing the chance of a favorable outcome. Therefore, the information considered and the decision rule used by the individual diverge from those prescribed by the decision reason. There is no indication that the individual prioritized the likelihood of a non-zero gain.",
